<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#bumiputera">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bumiputera</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bumiputera, 'sons of the soil', is the Malaysian term for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malays">Malays</a> and the indigenous peoples of the country, including the Orang Asli and the peoples of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabah">Sabah</a> and Sarawak. Article 153 of the constitution protects their special position, and since 1971 the New Economic Policy and its successors have given them preferences in education, public employment and business. They make up about seven in ten Malaysian citizens.</p></div>
